From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: keep the TX TID of a data frame in 0-7

ath11k_dp_tx_get_tid() hands skb->priority & 0xf to the TCL as the TID,
with TID override set. On the host path nothing reduces skb->priority to
an 802.1D tag first. 785 skips ieee80211_select_queue() for a
HAS_TX_QUEUE driver, which 456 makes ath11k in every mode. On an AP
interface the 802.3 path, ieee80211_8023_xmit_ap(), never calls it, and
the data netdevs have no ndo_select_queue. So whatever priority a frame
carries reaches the firmware, and a priority of 8-15 asserts its TX data
engine (ar_wal_tx_send.c:22193, WLAN_TX_DE) on the radio that sends the
frame.

Such a priority comes from ECM's uninitialised QoS tag on reply packets
of a UDP connection (qca-nss-ecm 0060 in nss-packages), and can come
from SO_PRIORITY or a tc skbedit or nft meta priority rule.

Mask with IEEE80211_QOS_CTL_TAG1D_MASK: 0-7 are unchanged, and the
256-263 form mac80211 uses to carry an 802.1D tag maps to the same TID.
QSDK pairs 785 with 335-0003, which turns TID override off instead and
leaves the TID to the hardware's DSCP classification. This tree has not
carried 335-0003 since mac80211 moved to Julius's patch set.

Signed-off-by: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
@@ -44,17 +44,22 @@ static void ath11k_dp_tx_encap_nwifi(str
 	hdr->frame_control &= ~__cpu_to_le16(IEEE80211_STYPE_QOS_DATA);
 }
 
+/* With the NSS mac80211 patches, skb->priority is not always reduced to
+ * an 802.1D tag before a frame gets here, and the firmware asserts on a
+ * data TID of 8-15. Keep the TID in 0-7; the 256-263 form mac80211 uses
+ * to carry a tag maps to the same TID.
+ */
 static u8 ath11k_dp_tx_get_tid(struct sk_buff *skb)
 {
 	struct ieee80211_hdr *hdr = (void *)skb->data;
 	struct ath11k_skb_cb *cb = ATH11K_SKB_CB(skb);
 
 	if (cb->flags & ATH11K_SKB_HW_80211_ENCAP)
-		return skb->priority & IEEE80211_QOS_CTL_TID_MASK;
+		return skb->priority & IEEE80211_QOS_CTL_TAG1D_MASK;
 	else if (!ieee80211_is_data_qos(hdr->frame_control))
 		return HAL_DESC_REO_NON_QOS_TID;
 	else
-		return skb->priority & IEEE80211_QOS_CTL_TID_MASK;
+		return skb->priority & IEEE80211_QOS_CTL_TAG1D_MASK;
 }
 
 enum hal_encrypt_type ath11k_dp_tx_get_encrypt_type(u32 cipher)
